# Tables that must be born with row-level security ENABLED on Postgres/Supabase.
# Supabase auto-exposes the `public` schema over PostgREST via the anon key; a
# table created RLS-disabled is world-readable/writable. The app connects as the
# owner role (BYPASSRLS), so enabling RLS with no policies locks out anon /
# authenticated while leaving the app untouched. This replaces the reactive
# boot-time ensure_rls() self-heal: tables are now born secure in the migration
# that creates them, so there is never an exposure window.
